message: "If you use this book, please cite it as below."
type: generic
title: "Bayesian Semiparametric Item Response Modelling for Person-Specific Latent Traits"
subtitle: "Theory, Identification, and the Literature Behind the Estimators"
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: JoonHo
    email: jlee296@ua.edu
    affiliation: "The University of Alabama"
abstract: >-
  The theory and literature companion of a research programme on Bayesian
  semiparametric item response modelling. It develops the measurement models
  and their identification, information and the reliability coefficients that
  summarise it, hierarchical shrinkage and its empirical-Bayes lineage,
  Dirichlet process mixture priors on the latent trait distribution, and the
  decision-theoretic case that three inferential goals — individual scores,
  ranks, and the trait distribution — imply three different posterior
  summaries. A focused part extends the argument to the two-parameter model,
  and a final part reads the realized evidence of the companion simulation and
  case-study volumes back into the theory.
keywords:
  - item response theory
  - psychometrics
  - Bayesian nonparametrics
  - Dirichlet process
  - Rasch model
  - reliability
  - identification
  - posterior summaries
